"\n  ],\n  \"evidence_refs\": [\n    \"paper_data.json#final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes/0/solution/summary/permuted_nonlinear/paired_widths/label_only\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"index\": 26,\n  \"claim\": \"permuted_nonlinear: frozen method versus ppi, ratio of mean widths 0.8710746293771102, stored ratio interval [0.8659673562031414, 0.8757820589989651], paired difference interval [-0.02623854197342319, -0.024106989324316073].\",\n  \"source_ids\": [\n    \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence_refs\": [\n    \"paper_data.json#final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes/0/solution/summary/permuted_nonlinear/paired_widths/ppi\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"index\": 27,\n  \"claim\": \"permuted_nonlinear: frozen method versus ppi_plus_plus, ratio of mean widths 1.018907315588936, stored ratio interval [1.0171814394192376, 1.0212178434481396], paired difference interval [0.0028564239519265834, 0.00352876463176102].\",\n  \"source_ids\": [\n    \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence_refs\": [\n    \"paper_data.json#final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes/0/solution/summary/permuted_nonlinear/paired_widths/ppi_plus_plus\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"index\": 28,\n  \"claim\": \"Gene-expression mean width reduction versus PPI++ is 5.693037791600409 percent; it is narrower than all three references. All six other conditions have strictly positive paired width-difference intervals versus PPI++.\",\n  \"source_ids\": [\n    \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence_refs\": [\n    \"analysis_summary.json\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"index\": 29,\n  \"claim\": \"Frozen-method condition-wise coverage ranges from 0.95 to 0.98; all simultaneous lower endpoints are below 0.95. No point estimate or qualification establishes a finite-sample coverage theorem.\",\n  \"source_ids\": [\n    \"final.evidence.episodes\",\n    \"final.metric.empirical_coverage\",\n    \"final.metric.minimum_case_coverage\",\n    \"final.metric.nominal_coverage\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence_refs\": [\n    \"analysis_summary.json\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"index\": 30,\n  \"claim\": \"Final assessment completed, with outcome qualified and no recorded failures; scientific-validity value zero is conservative non-certification, not evidence of a diagnosed coverage or adaptivity failure.\",\n  \"source_ids\": [\n    \"final.qualification.status\",\n    \"final.qualification.outcome\",\n    \"final.qualification.correct\",\n    \"final.metric.failure_fraction\",\n    \"final.metric.scientific_validity\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence_refs\": [\n    \"paper_data.json#final_evaluation\",\n    \"source_evidence/resource_manifest.json#scientific_limits\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"index\": 31,\n  \"claim\": \"Final assessment: 400 seeds 1000 through 1399, seven conditions, nominal coverage 0.95, 128 labeled observations and 8192 unlabeled scores per condition; all methods have paired inputs.\",\n  \"source_ids\": [\n    \"final.evidence.episodes\",\n    \"final.metric.nominal_coverage\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence_refs\": [\n    \"source_evidence/evaluate_final.py#L861-L895\",\n    \"source_evidence/resource_manifest.json#raw_shapes\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"index\": 32,\n  \"claim\": \"Stored reporting protocol: simultaneous Clopper-Pearson coverage bounds over seven conditions and four methods; 512 paired bootstrap resamples with random seed 79231 and width comparison quantiles at 0.05/42 and 1-0.05/42.\",\n  \"source_ids\": [\n    \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence_refs\": [\n    \"source_evidence/evaluate_final.py#L920-L974\",\n    \"source_evidence/resource_manifest.json#uncertainty\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"index\": 33,\n  \"claim\": \"Synthetic targets: linear and uninformative 0.5, nonlinear 0.1+0.8/3, rare outcome 0.01+0.08/3. Constant and permuted controls reuse nonlinear outcomes; constant scores equal 0.5. Gene-expression target is the mean of the final unique-record empirical source, not external biological truth.\",\n  \"source_ids\": [\n    \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence_refs\": [\n    \"source_evidence/evaluate_final.py#L861-L895\",\n    \"source_evidence/resource_manifest.json#source\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"index\": 34,\n  \"claim\": \"Reported main estimand is ratio of mean widths; secondary per-repetition ratio aggregate is capped at 100 and is not interpreted as a percentage width increase. Five rare-outcome PPI++ intervals have zero width.\",\n  \"source_ids\": [\n    \"final.evidence.episodes\",\n    \"final.metric.mean_width_ratio\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence_refs\": [\n    \"analysis_summary.json\",\n    \"source_evidence/evaluate_final.py\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"index\": 35,\n  \"claim\": \"Selected readable source uses K=min(5,floor(n/2)) outer folds, three shared inner folds, zero/affine/nonlinear selection, and no unlabeled values in fitting or selection. The selection record identifies the inspected source location; source content, not the score or tree digest, supports these details. Independently verified byte identity to the final frozen tree is not asserted.\",\n  \"source_ids\": [\n    \"result.top_program_01\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence_refs\": [\n    \"source_evidence/program.py#L154-L267\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"index\": 36,\n  \"claim\": \"Nonlinear basis contains linear, quadratic and positive-part terms at normalized knots -0.5, 0, 0.5; diagonal ridge penalties 0.1, 2, 4, 4, 4; training quantiles 0.1, 0.9; binary calibrations clipped before signed multiplier. The selection record identifies the inspected source location; source content, not the score or tree digest, supports these details. Independently verified byte identity to the final frozen tree is not asserted.\",\n  \"source_ids\": [\n    \"result.top_program_01\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence_refs\": [\n    \"source_evidence/program.py#L69-L151\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"index\": 37,\n  \"claim\": \"Finite-N multiplier uses covariance divided by (1+n/N) times control variance; inner criterion adds residual variance and n/N times control variance; paired excess-risk plus one standard error must be negative. The selection record identifies the inspected source location; source content, not the score or tree digest, supports these details. Independently verified byte identity to the final frozen tree is not asserted.\",\n  \"source_ids\": [\n    \"result.top_program_01\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence_refs\": [\n    \"source_evidence/program.py#L154-L200\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"index\": 38,\n  \"claim\": \"Returned moments center residuals within folds and take the variance of the weighted combined controls on the shared unlabeled pool, including cross-fold covariance. The selection record identifies the inspected source location; source content, not the score or tree digest, supports these details. Independently verified byte identity to the final frozen tree is not asserted.\",\n  \"source_ids\": [\n    \"result.top_program_01\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence_refs\": [\n    \"source_evidence/program.py#L215-L267\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"index\": 39,\n  \"claim\": \"Student critical value has max(2,n-6) degrees of freedom; binary endpoints are clipped; constant scores and binary counts with fewer than ten successes or failures use label-only inference. The selection record identifies the inspected source location; source content, not the score or tree digest, supports these details. Independently verified byte identity to the final frozen tree is not asserted.\",\n  \"source_ids\": [\n    \"result.top_program_01\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence_refs\": [\n    \"source_evidence/program.py#L270-L305\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"index\": 40,\n  \"claim\": \"Internal bounded certificate uses alpha/(2K) allocation, signed control bounds and a variance-sensitive bounded-mean radius; it is not the returned interval. The selection record identifies the inspected source location; source content, not the score or tree digest, supports these details. Independently verified byte identity to the final frozen tree is not asserted.\",\n  \"source_ids\": [\n    \"result.top_program_01\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence_refs\": [\n    \"source_evidence/program.py#L201-L305\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"index\": 41,\n  \"claim\": \"Deterministic control and fixed-fold variance identities, oracle nonlinear/affine headroom identities, and fold-offset invariance hold within their stated moment and independence assumptions; learned-fold coverage additionally requires stability and a common deterministic L2 limit. The selection record identifies the inspected source location; source content, not the score or tree digest, supports these details. Independently verified byte identity to the final frozen tree is not asserted.\",\n  \"source_ids\": [\n    \"result.top_program_01\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence_refs\": [\n    \"source_evidence/METHOD.md#L80-L183\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"index\": 42,\n  \"claim\": \"Reference mean intervals use ppi-python 0.2.3, lam=1 versus lam=None, optimized coefficient clipped to [0,1], and normal-approximation mean intervals; sample-variance and return conventions differ from the frozen method.\",\n  \"source_ids\": [\n    \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence_refs\": [\n    \"source_evidence/evaluate_final.py#L754-L809\",\n    \"source_evidence/ppi.py#L135-L229\",\n    \"source_evidence/ppi.py#L1754-L1825\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"index\": 43,\n  \"claim\": \"No controlled component ablation or additional task results are supplied; information controls are not component ablations. Observed configuration differences do not identify which component caused the empirical-source gain.\",\n  \"source_ids\": [\n    \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence_refs\": [\n    \"paper_data.json#ablation_studies\",\n    \"paper_data.json#final_evaluation\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"index\": 44,\n  \"claim\": \"Original declared environment and analysis-only figure environment use NumPy 1.26.4 and SciPy 1.12.0; Matplotlib figure version is 3.8.4; full original declarations are preserved without claiming they were all installed.\",\n  \"source_ids\": [\n    \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence_refs\": [\n    \"source_evidence/requirements.txt