{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"rg -n 'nonlinear|headroom|conditional' source_evidence/test_controls.py paper_strategy.md paper_strategy.json; sed -n '288,311p' paper_evidence_audit_packet.md; jq '{keys:keys,reference_validation, supplementary_information_validation}' validation_report.json\"","aggregated_output":"paper_strategy.json:6:  \"central_thesis\": \"The frozen risk-adaptive control method yields narrower mean intervals than PPI and PPI++ on the evaluated empirical gene-expression source, but is wider than PPI++ in all six synthetic or perturbed-score conditions; observed coverage and offset-invariant studentization support a conditional efficiency study, not universal narrowing or a finite-sample validity certificate.\",\npaper_strategy.json:7:  \"narrative_rationale\": \"One shared question connects the real scalar table, synthetic conditions, and score perturbations. The completed final evaluation supplies 400 paired repeats per condition, interval endpoints, baseline coverage, and stored uncertainty summaries. A direct condition-by-comparator view is scientifically stronger than a search-score story: the selected method has aggregate coverage 0.9610714285714286, minimum condition coverage 0.95, and a reported capped mean episode width ratio of 1.2106794607646876. The gene-expression paired width-difference interval versus PPI++ is [-0.02969064263718976, -0.02435572792761422], whereas the corresponding differences are positive in the other six conditions. Qualification is completed/qualified/true in final.qualification.*, independently of the absent downstream_study. The conservative scientific_validity field is explicitly fixed to zero by the local evaluator, so it is neither evidence of an identified validity failure nor a certificate. Theoretical headroom and offset invariance explain the design space, not the measured cause of the real-table gain. No component ablation identifies that cause.\",\npaper_strategy.json:15:    \"ablation_studies is empty and its evidence directory is missing. Existing search variants may support a clearly separated exploratory supplement, but cannot establish the causal contribution of nonlinear fitting, risk selection, or studentization.\",\npaper_strategy.json:38:      \"include_reason\": \"They reuse the nonlinear records under specified score transformations and test dependence on score information without changing the method. Present alongside the independently uninformative condition; do not call them isolated ablations of calibration or variance estimation.\"\npaper_strategy.json:44:    \"Boundary of benefit: every other condition has a positive paired mean-width difference versus PPI++; the nonlinear condition itself does not show a benefit. Distinguish improvement relative to label-only or unoptimized PPI from improvement relative to PPI++.\",\npaper_strategy.json:48:    \"Mechanistic scope: deterministic-control finite-N variance/headroom identities and fold-offset invariance are explanatory algebra. Overlapping fitted folds, heuristic family selection, critical-value differences, clipping, and fallbacks prevent attributing the measured width change to one component without unavailable controlled ablations.\"\npaper_strategy.json:84:      \"layout_rationale\": \"Two vertically stacked panels at 5.5 inches wide, approximately 3.3-3.7 inches tall in total, use a common log-ratio axis and reference at one. Panel one contains gene expression, linear, nonlinear, and rare outcomes; panel two contains uninformative, constant-score, and permuted-score conditions. Three offset point/interval series identify label-only, PPI, and PPI++ comparators. Stacking avoids illegible labels in half-width panels. Reserve about half a page including caption; minimum rendered text 8pt, preferably 9pt. State that a width advantage alone is not a coverage advantage.\",\npaper_strategy.json:113:        \"grounded_content\": \"Expand the inspected selected src/METHOD.md and src/program.py into deterministic-control finite-N variance, oracle affine/nonlinear headroom, and fold-offset cancellation derivations. Include the weighted shared-pool covariance terms, nested family-selection details, signed multipliers, spline penalties, t critical value, clipping, and fallback rules. State assumptions separately for deterministic controls and learned cross-fit asymptotics. Do not claim the sufficient stability assumptions were verified empirically, and do not report unexecuted test_controls.py as a passed test.\",\npaper_strategy.json:163:    \"the nonlinear component caused the observed gain\",\npaper_strategy.json:181:    \"Resource fixing is within each matched replicate. Repeated sampling changes the labeled and unlabeled draws; coverage is not conditional on every observed input being fixed. For the real source the target is its normalized empirical-source mean, not an external biological population. Only scalar predictions/outcomes are observed; no new backbone, promoter-feature, or sequence-disjointness claim is supported.\",\npaper_strategy.json:182:    \"Explain the estimator as a weighted held-out residual mean plus a shared-unlabeled control mean. Explain offset invariance without claiming pooled residual studentization empirically failed. The deterministic variance identity does not become an exact conditional variance formula for overlapping learned folds. The inner-fold excess-risk uncertainty is a selection heuristic, not a calibrated hypothesis test.\",\npaper_strategy.md:11:**Central thesis:** The frozen risk-adaptive control method yields narrower mean intervals than PPI and PPI++ on the evaluated empirical gene-expression source, but is wider than PPI++ in all six synthetic or perturbed-score conditions. Observed coverage and offset-invariant studentization support a conditional efficiency study, not universal narrowing or a finite-sample validity certificate.\npaper_strategy.md:38:| Preserve a prospective nonlinear saturation/certificate success story | Reject: oracle identities are available, but the reported interval is not the internal certificate, and nonlinear synthetic data do not show a width benefit against PPI++. |\npaper_strategy.md:43:The final evidence changes the private source-only perspective into a measured conditional-results story. No inherited title or figure plan is retained by inertia. Constant/permuted scores support the shared question without becoming independent natural datasets. This structure transfers to other tasks by selecting the frozen method, retaining valid matched references, and organizing conditions by the boundaries they test rather than by execution order.\npaper_strategy.md:50:4. **Supporting conditions: constant and permuted scores.** These perturb the nonlinear records, complementing the uninformative condition. They are information controls, not isolated ablations of nonlinear calibration or studentization.\npaper_strategy.md:56:Use every final condition: gene expression, linear, nonlinear, rare outcomes, uninformative, constant-score nonlinear, and permuted-score nonlinear. Group the first four as predictive conditions and the last three as information controls. All required comparison figures use this same partition.\npaper_strategy.md:60:**Boundary of benefit.** All six other conditions have positive paired width-difference intervals versus PPI++. Preserve these results in the main paper, including the explicitly nonlinear condition. Gains against label-only inference or PPI do not imply gains against PPI++.\npaper_strategy.md:68:**Mechanism without causal overreach.** Explain deterministic-control finite-N headroom and offset cancellation, but do not attribute the measured gain to nonlinear fitting, selection, or studentization individually. No final component ablations exist. Critical values, clipping, and fallbacks also differ between methods.\npaper_strategy.md:76:Separate deterministic-control 